# Corpus unit pinn/C05 — gap (an unmatched tuning budget breaks baseline parity)
#
# Source: pinn C05 annotation (comparative, controlled_comparison; corpus pin 62e9b54).
# Headline: Adam+L-BFGS consistently outperforms Adam or L-BFGS alone — min L2RE 14.2x smaller
# than Adam on convection and 6.07x smaller than L-BFGS on wave, and per (PDE, width) cell it
# attains the lowest min loss and L2RE, with reaction at width 100 the acknowledged exception
# (E03, Table 1).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * controlled_comparison: conclusion better(adam_lbfgs, adam, min_l2re, pinn_pdes). Nearest-
#     competitor convention takes Adam (the tuned, closest competitor; reaction@width=100 is
#     where Adam ties) as B; L-BFGS-alone, the two effect sizes (14.2x, 6.07x), and the reaction
#     exception stay in nl and refs.
#   * The mandatory baseline_parity CQ is unmet-gap: the setups are not matched on tuning effort —
#     Adam searches 5 lrs, Adam+L-BFGS searches 5 lrs x 3 switch points = 15 configs, and L-BFGS
#     alone is untuned (lr=1.0); selecting the best configuration per optimizer then favors the
#     larger grid. The controlled_comparison argument is declared as a located hole with
#     `open baseline_parity` (lowering re-done for issue #15 under lara-core@0.3; until
#     lara-core@0.2 the open mandatory obligation rejected the unit, so the arg was omitted): it
#     is not an AF node and the claim stays gap on empty complete support. The annotation rates
#     this CQ unmet-GAP (not unmet-defeater) and every trace dead end is decision:none, so the
#     tuning asymmetry is a hole, not a licensed undercut — the unit stays a gap, not defeated.
#   * The gap here is baseline_parity, not variance: variance_reported IS met (E03 reports 5
#     seeds, min/median/max) and measurement_validity is met (min L2RE a standard metric; the
#     14.2x/6.07x ratios are arithmetic re-checks against Table 1). Both are discharged on the
#     hole. The optional scope_match has no annotated basis and is opened (R5 question
#     accounting; no status effect).
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact pinn at sha256:116d458ce7eb
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------------------

claim c05
  nl      = "Adam+L-BFGS consistently outperforms Adam or L-BFGS alone: min L2RE 14.2x smaller than Adam on convection and 6.07x smaller than L-BFGS on wave, and the lowest min loss and L2RE per (PDE, width) cell, except reaction at width 100 where Adam is comparable"
  formal  = better(adam_lbfgs, adam, min_l2re, pinn_pdes)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: Table 1's per-cell min-loss/L2RE orderings and the two ratio cells, per
# result cell, folded into refs.
leaf e1 : reports(e03, compares(adam_lbfgs, adam, min_l2re, pinn_pdes, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [Table-1, Figure-8, section-6.1, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N08]

leaf e2 : valid_measurement(min_l2re, e03)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [Table-1, logic/experiments.md#E03-Setup]

leaf e3 : variance_reported(e03)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-Setup, logic/experiments.md#E03-Procedure-step-6]

# --- ... but only an incomplete argument (a located hole) is declarable -------------------------

# The incomplete argument: baseline_parity has no honest leaf — the tuning budgets are
# asymmetric (untuned L-BFGS, 5-config Adam, 15-config Adam+L-BFGS) — and corpus-v1 makes it
# mandatory, so it stays open and a1 is a hole.
arg a1 : supports(c05) by controlled_comparison(adam_lbfgs, adam, min_l2re, pinn_pdes, e03)
  discharge measurement_validity with e2
  discharge variance_reported    with e3
  open      baseline_parity
  open      scope_match

status c05

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments (a1 is a located hole, not an AF node).
# Located hole: a1 (controlled_comparison), open obligations [baseline_parity];
#   sources no attacks.
# Claim status:
#   c05 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8;
#          the hole a1 is reported in the verdict's holes section, not as a node)
